// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list, inclusive), then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this position was null, or it is equal to the old element at this position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the original element was null, or equals the original element at that position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent position is either null and was null before, or is equal to the element that was at the previous position before the insertion.
